    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const ctx = $input.first().json;\n\nconst message = $('Validate input').first().json.message;\nconst session_id = $('Validate input').first().json.session_id;\n\nconst history = Array.isArray(ctx.conversation_history)\n  ? ctx.conversation_history\n  : JSON.parse(ctx.conversation_history ?? '[]');\n\nconst systemPrompt = `You are a research assistant embedded in a haptic feedback research application.\n\nCurrent experiment: ${ctx.usecase_name ?? 'Unknown'}\n${ctx.usecase_description ? `Description: ${ctx.usecase_description}` : ''}\n\nActive feedback mappings for this experiment:\n${JSON.stringify(ctx.global_mappings ?? [], null, 2)}\n\nYour job is to help researchers with ONE of the following tasks. Decide which one applies to the message, then respond ONLY with a JSON object in this exact format:\n\n{\n  \"intent\": \"<one of: mapping | knowledge | dictionary | scheduling | usecase_builder | clarify>\",\n  \"reply\": \"<your response to the researcher in plain language>\",\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"action\": \"<for mapping intent: list | add | remove | brainstorm>\",\n    \"params\": {}\n  }\n}\n\nIntent rules:\n- \"mapping\"        → researcher wants to view, add, remove, or brainstorm feedback_config_rules\n- \"knowledge\"      → question about haptic feedback, sensory substitution, or experiment design\n- \"dictionary\" → researcher wants to see use cases, add/delete use cases, or modify parameters. Those use cases are not yet integrated in the system, but are a potential for addition in the future.\n- \"scheduling\"→ researcher wants to add, list (Either the active ones all all of them, the default is to list all), deactivate, activate, or change user schedules\n- \"usecase_builder\" → researcher wants to create, configure, generate code for, or receive implementation instructions for adding a new API-based use case to the Vibration Orchestrator template.\n- \"clarify\"        → message is ambiguous, you need to ask one follow-up question\n\nPayload rules by intent:\n- mapping + list:       { \"action\": \"list\", \"params\": {} }\n- mapping + add:        { \"action\": \"add\", \"params\": { \"minvalue\": 80, \"maxvalue\": 100, \"minpulses\": 3, \"maxpulses\": 5, \"minintensity\": 60, \"maxintensity\": 80, \"minduration\": 200, \"maxduration\": 300, \"mininterval\": 100, \"maxinterval\": 150 } }\n- mapping + add: ALWAYS route to \"add\" even if you think the mapping already exists. \n  The database will handle duplicate detection and inform the user. Never route to \"list\" \n  when the researcher is asking to add something.\n- mapping + remove:     { \"action\": \"remove\", \"params\": { \"id\": 123 } } — ONLY when researcher gives explicit numeric ID\n- mapping + brainstorm: { \"action\": \"brainstorm\", \"params\": {} }\n- all others:           { \"action\": \"\", \"params\": {} }\n\nPayload rules for scheduling:\n- \"add\": { \"action\": \"add\", \"params\": { \"user_id\": 101, \"interval_days\": 2, \"measure_type\": \"average\", \"trigger_percentage\": 20 } }\n- \"change\": { \"action\": \"change\", \"params\": { \"schedule_id\": 1, \"user_id\": 101, \"interval_days\": 3, \"measure_type\": \"average\", \"trigger_percentage\": 0.25 } }\n- \"deactivate\": { \"action\": \"deactivate\", \"params\": { \"schedule_id\": 1 } }\n- \"activate\" : { \"action\": \"activate\", \"params\": { \"schedule_id\": 1 } }\n- \"listActive\": { \"action\": \"listActive\", \"params\": {} }\n- \"listAll\": { \"action\": \"listAll\", \"params\": {} }\n\nPayload rules for dictionary intent:\n- list: { \"action\": \"list\", \"params\": {} }\n- add: { \"action\": \"add\", \"params\": { \"usecase_name\": \"\", \"usecase_parameter_name\": \"\", \"parameter_format\": \"\", \"is_required\": true, \"description\": \"\" } }\n- delete usecase: { \"action\": \"remove_usecase\", \"params\": { \"usecase_name\": \"\" } }\n- delete parameter: { \"action\": \"remove_parameter\", \"params\": { \"dict_entry\": 123,\"usecase_name\": \"\", \"usecase_parameter_name\": \"\" } }\n- edit: { \"action\": \"edit\", \"params\": { \"dict_entry\": 123, \"usecase_name\": \"\", \"usecase_parameter_name\": \"\", \"parameter_format\": \"\", \"is_required\": True,\"Description\":\"\"(optional) } }\n\nPayload rules for usecase_builder:\n- generate template code:\n{\n  \"action\": \"generate_template_code\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"usecase_name\": \"\",\n    \"api_name\": \"\",\n    \"api_id\": null,\n    \"measurement_name\": \"\",\n    \"response_value_path\": \"\",\n    \"context\": \"\"\n  }\n}\n\nUse this intent when the researcher says things like:\n- create a new use case\n- add a new API-based use case\n- generate the code for the template nodes\n- help me configure the Vibration Orchestrator template\n- use an API from the API pool for a new use case\n- create a workflow for a new API\n\nIf the researcher provides a use case/API name, copy it into both usecase_name and api_name unless they clearly describe different names.\nIf the researcher provides the measured value, copy it into measurement_name.\nIf the researcher provides a JSON path in the API response, copy it into response_value_path.\nIf the researcher does not provide response_value_path, leave it as an empty string.\nIf the researcher does not provide api_id, set api_id to null.\nThe context field should summarize what the researcher wants to monitor and why.\n\nIMPORTANT: For \"add\", ALWAYS set action to \"add\" and extract ALL numeric values from the \nmessage into params. Do NOT second-guess whether the mapping exists — always send it to \nthe add workflow regardless. The system handles duplicates automatically.\nIMPORTANT: \"add\" and \"remove\" are completely different. Adding range values is ALWAYS \"add\". \"remove\" needs an explicit ID.\n\nDo not respond with anything outside the JSON object.`;\n\nconst messages = [\n  { role: 'system', content: systemPrompt },\n  ...history,\n  { role: 'user', content: message }\n];\n\nconst messagesAsText = messages.map(m => {\n  const role = m.role === 'system' ? 'SYSTEM' : m.role === 'assistant' ? 'ASSISTANT' : 'USER';\n  return `${role}: ${m.content}`;\n}).join('\\n\\n');\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    session_id,\n    message,\n    messages,\n    messages_as_text: messagesAsText,\n    usecase_name:    ctx.usecase_name,\n    usecase_id:      ctx.usecase_id,\n    global_mappings: ctx.global_mappings,\n    history\n  }\n}];"
      },
